            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "fastbettyxxx"
            },
            "reviewBody": "really tasty... and hubby said he liked it better than his moms recipe! I used this recipe and basically just doubled some of the ingredients and threw it all in a crockpot. I threw my frozen meatballs, Worcestershire sauce, beef stock, and rosemary all in a crockpot on high for 3 hours. I sprayed the crock with a non-stick spray first. I stirred about once an hour. Then I added to the meatballs in the crock another 1/2 cup beef stock, 3 more tsp Worcestershire sauce, pepper to taste, garlic salt (a pinch), another 1/2 tsp rosemary. I mixed together 2 cups cream and 6 tbsp flour and poured that in the crock. I let all that cook on high for another hour. It thickened up really nice.",
            "datePublished": "2018-06-26T23:43:27.100Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
