            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PlumLadle7712"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made the sauce according to the recipe, but only had low sodium soy sauce. I was worried it might get lumpy using all purpose flour, so I used a balloon whisk to stir it. It thickened beautifully with no lumps. When I tasted it at the end of cooking I thought it was a little bland, so I added salt and a pinch of ground nutmeg. Delicious with frozen cooked meatballs warmed in the air fryer, over eggs noodles with extra ground pepper. I’m going to try left over sauce with sliced cooked mushrooms, which I think would work great. Very easy recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-31T00:23:38.021Z"
          },
          {
